---
import GuideArticle from '../layouts/GuideArticle.astro'; import { citer } from '../lib/cite.js'; import { bySlug, pricingCurated } from '../lib/data.js';
const { c, used, U } = citer();
const keys = Object.keys(pricingCurated).filter(k=>!k.startsWith('_')&&bySlug[k]);
const row = k => { const p=pricingCurated[k], e=bySlug[k]; return `<tr><td data-l="Product" class="nm"><a href="/agents/${k}/">${e.name}</a><br/><span class="muted small">${e.maker||U}</span></td><td data-l="Price">${p.price.replace(/unknown/g,U)}${c('ps-'+k)}</td><td data-l="Confirmed on pricing page?">${p.confirmed?'Yes':'No, from another official source'}</td><td data-l="Checked" class="mono">${p.checked}</td></tr>`; };
const personal = keys.filter(k=>bySlug[k].category==='personal').map(row).join('');
const managed = keys.filter(k=>bySlug[k].category==='managed').map(row).join('');
const sessHr = 0.08, hrs = 8*22;
const body = `
<div class="tldr"><p><b>Short answer.</b> For one person, an AI agent costs <b>$0–20 a month</b> for most needs, and <b>$100–200</b> if you hand it hours of work a day. For a team, budget <b>$20–30 per seat per month</b>. Open-source agents are free software, but you pay for the AI model behind them. Running your own agents on a cloud platform is metered: tokens plus compute by the hour.</p></div>

<h2>The three ways you pay</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Flat subscription</b> (ChatGPT, Claude, Grok Bot, Gemini, Muse): a monthly price with usage limits. Simple to budget.</li>
<li><b>Credits</b> (Manus, Lindy): each task burns credits. Manus Pro starts at $20 for 4,000 credits${c('mn-pricing')}; Lindy starts at $29.99 for 3,000 and pauses when you run out, unless you top up at $10 per 1,000${c('ly')}.</li>
<li><b>Metered</b> (agent platforms for builders): you pay model tokens plus runtime. Claude Managed Agents, for example, is model tokens plus $0.08 per session-hour${c('ps-claude-managed-agents')}.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Personal AI agents: every price we track</h2>
<p>From our pricing data. Each price links to the vendor's own page; "No" in the confirmed column means the number wasn't visible in the fetched pricing-page text (blocked or rendered by script) and comes from another official page, so treat it as unconfirmed.</p>
<div class="gtable-wrap"><table class="gtab"><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Price</th><th>Confirmed on pricing page?</th><th>Checked</th></tr></thead><tbody>${personal}</tbody></table></div>
<p class="muted small">Notes: Meta's subscriptions help page lists Muse at free with limits, Power $20/mo and Maximum $100/mo${c('mu')}, newer than the App Store listing above. ChatGPT Plus is $20/mo and Pro comes at $100 or $200/mo, with a $500 Pro tier added in September${c('oai-rn')}. Claude's Max tier runs from $100/mo${c('cl-pricing')}.</p>

<h2>For teams: price per seat</h2>
<div class="gtable-wrap"><table class="gtab"><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Per seat / mo</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td data-l="Plan" class="nm">ChatGPT Business</td><td data-l="Per seat / mo" class="mono">$20–25</td><td data-l="Notes">Annual vs monthly; Premium $100–125${c('oai-biz2')}</td></tr>
<tr><td data-l="Plan" class="nm">Claude Team</td><td data-l="Per seat / mo" class="mono">$20–25</td><td data-l="Notes">Annual vs monthly; Premium $100–125${c('cl-team2')}</td></tr>
<tr><td data-l="Plan" class="nm">Gemini Enterprise (Business)</td><td data-l="Per seat / mo" class="mono">from $21</td><td data-l="Notes">${c('g-ent')}</td></tr>
<tr><td data-l="Plan" class="nm">Microsoft 365 Copilot Business</td><td data-l="Per seat / mo" class="mono">$21</td><td data-l="Notes">Add-on; needs a Microsoft 365 business plan; $18 promo to Dec 31, 2026${c('ms-price')}</td></tr>
<tr><td data-l="Plan" class="nm">Manus Team</td><td data-l="Per seat / mo" class="mono">from $20</td><td data-l="Notes">Credit-based${c('mn-pricing')}</td></tr>
<tr><td data-l="Plan" class="nm">Grok Bot team seat</td><td data-l="Per seat / mo" class="mono">$30–200</td><td data-l="Notes">Same as Premium, Super, Ultra${c('gb-pricing')}</td></tr>
<tr><td data-l="Plan" class="nm">Perplexity Enterprise Pro</td><td data-l="Per seat / mo" class="mono">$40</td><td data-l="Notes">Or $400/yr${c('px-ent')}</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Ten people on ChatGPT Business or Claude Team at the annual rate is $2,400 a year; at the monthly rate, $3,000. More detail in the <a href="/best-ai-agent-for-small-business/">small-business guide</a>.</p>

<h2>Running your own agents: platform prices</h2>
<p>If you're building agents rather than subscribing to one, you pay a platform. These prices exclude model tokens unless stated.</p>
<div class="gtable-wrap"><table class="gtab"><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Price</th><th>Confirmed on pricing page?</th><th>Checked</th></tr></thead><tbody>${managed}</tbody></table></div>
<p><b>Worked example:</b> one Claude Managed Agents session running 8 hours a day, 22 working days a month, is ${hrs} session-hours × $${sessHr} = <b>$${(hrs*sessHr).toFixed(2)}</b> a month in runtime${c('ps-claude-managed-agents')}, plus the model tokens it uses. Token costs depend on the model and the workload, so the total for your use case is ${U} until you measure it.</p>

<h2>Hidden costs to budget for</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Shared pools.</b> Grok Bot usage comes out of a weekly pool shared with Grok and Cursor${c('gb-docs')}.</li>
<li><b>Required base licences.</b> Copilot Business needs a Microsoft 365 business plan and an annual commitment${c('ms-price','ms-biz')}.</li>
<li><b>Gated features.</b> Gemini Agent requires Google AI Ultra ($99.99 or $199.99/mo) and is US and English only${c('g-plans')}. ChatGPT dots need Pro or Business Premium${c('oai-rn')}.</li>
<li><b>Overage.</b> ChatGPT Business and Claude Team both sell extra usage credits beyond the included limits${c('oai-biz2','cl-team2')}.</li>
<li><b>Open-source isn't $0.</b> OpenClaw has no subscription or hosted tier${c('oc')}, and Hermes Agent's optional Nous Portal tiers sell model credits${c('hm')}. You still pay a model provider and spend time on setup and security (see <a href="/is-openclaw-safe/">Is OpenClaw safe?</a>).</li>
</ul>

<h2>How to keep the bill sane</h2>
<ol>
<li>Start on monthly billing; switch to annual (about 20% cheaper on ChatGPT and Claude seats${c('oai-biz2','cl-team2')}) after two months of real use.</li>
<li>Give Premium seats only to the people who hit limits. Both ChatGPT Business and Claude Team let you mix seat types${c('oai-biz2','cl-team2')}.</li>
<li>For credit plans, set a monthly cap and check usage weekly.</li>
</ol>
<p>Prices change. We re-check vendor pages weekly and log changes on the <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> and in the <a href="/guide/">buyer's guide</a>.</p>
`;
const faqs = [
 ['How much does an AI agent cost per month?',`For one person, $0–20 covers most needs: ChatGPT Plus and Claude Pro are $20${c('oai-rn','cl-pricing')}. Heavy users pay $100–200 (ChatGPT Pro, Claude Max, Grok Bot via X Super or Ultra)${c('oai-rn','cl-pricing','gb-pricing')}.`],
 ['How much does an AI agent cost for a business?',`About $20–30 per seat per month. ChatGPT Business and Claude Team are $20 annual or $25 monthly per seat${c('oai-biz2','cl-team2')}; Copilot Business is $21 on top of Microsoft 365${c('ms-price')}.`],
 ['Are open-source AI agents free?',`The software is: OpenClaw and Hermes Agent are MIT-licensed${c('oc','hm')}. You still pay for the AI model you connect and for hosting if you don't run it on your own computer.`],
 ['What is the cheapest AI agent?',`Several have free tiers: Claude, Manus and Muse among them${c('ps-claude-app','mn-pricing','mu')}. OpenClaw costs nothing for the software${c('oc')}. Free tiers have tight limits.`],
 ['What does it cost to run my own AI agents in the cloud?',`Metered. Claude Managed Agents is tokens plus $0.08 per session-hour${c('ps-claude-managed-agents')}; Google's agent platform lists $0.085 per vCPU-hour${c('ps-vertex-agent-engine')}; AWS Bedrock AgentCore runtime lists $0.0895 per vCPU-hour${c('ps-bedrock-agentcore')}.`],
];
---
<GuideArticle slug="how-much-does-an-ai-agent-cost" kicker="Cost"
 title="How Much Does an AI Agent Cost? (2026 Price Table) | AgentStackWatch"
 desc="What AI agents cost in 2026: a sourced price table for ChatGPT, Claude, Grok Bot, Manus, Lindy, Gemini, Muse, OpenClaw and more, per-seat business prices, cloud agent platform rates and hidden costs."
 h1="How much does an AI agent cost? (2026)"
 dek="Every personal agent we track, its price and where it's from, plus per-seat business costs, what it costs to run your own agents, and the hidden extras."
 faqs={faqs} used={used}
 related={[['/compare/grok-bot-vs-chatgpt-dots/','Grok Bot vs ChatGPT dots'],['/compare/manus-vs-lindy/','Manus vs Lindy'],['/compare/claude-managed-agents-vs-openai-agents-api/','Claude Managed Agents vs OpenAI Agents API'],['/compare/vertex-agent-engine-vs-bedrock-agentcore/','Vertex Agent Engine vs Bedrock AgentCore'],['/best-free-ai-agent/','Best free AI agents and assistants (what you get for $0)']]}>
<Fragment set:html={body}/>
</GuideArticle>
